      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Unfortunately there is currently no way that the SteamVR API exposes to get information on which \"trackers\" are actually hand tracked devices.\n\nAs a workaround, you can ignore relevant serial numbers as trackers. E.g. for Virtual Desktop, try this launch parameter: `--ignore-trackers=HANDL,HANDR`.\n\nIn a future update I might change it so that this also disables the visual representation that annoyingly follows your hands when you have the Main Menu open.\n\nClosing this as it is not possible to implement fully as requested for now.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-07-31T04:20:48.605Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Repro steps:\n\n1. Use OpenVR-SpaceCalibrator to run both index controllers (lighthouse) drivers (with vive or tundra trackers) and Virtual Desktop/quest drivers at the same time.\n\n2. In VRChat, try to calibrate FBT with the index controllers turned on\n\nIf you do this, your hand tracking points will be recognized as trackers and bound to arbitrary points on your avatar (e.g. shoulders). As a workaround, turning off the index controllers before calibrating avoids the issue.\n\nAs an aside, I'm not sure how well supported this dual-controller setup is. That being said, this is the only major problem I've found with it so far - it's very convenient to be able to switch between hand tracking when I want expressiveness and index controllers when I want to use XSOverlay or manipulate menus. So it'd be nice to be able to do something about this one minor issue.",
